# Folder Structure (Standard Layout)

```
app/
├── Actions/
├── Http/Controllers/       # Api/ for API controllers
├── Http/Requests/
├── Http/Resources/
├── Jobs/
├── Livewire/
├── Models/
├── Policies/
├── Repositories/
│   ├── Contracts/
│   └── Eloquent/
├── Rules/
└── Services/
```

Do not introduce `app/Domain/` unless the project explicitly migrates to DDD. Do not mix layouts.

## Layer Rules

| Layer | Does | Must NOT |
|-------|------|----------|
| Controller / Livewire | I/O, delegate | Business logic, raw SQL, validation rules |
| Form Request | Validate / authorize input | DB writes, side effects |
| Action | Single `__invoke` operation | Unrelated multi-ops |
| Service | Coordinated business logic | HTTP, Blade, raw SQL |
| Repository | Eloquent / QB / raw SQL | HTTP, mail, cache, business rules |
| Model | Relations, scopes, casts | Mail, uploads, complex raw SQL |
| Resource | API shaping | Queries |

## Placement

- API controllers → `Http/Controllers/Api/`
- Feature tests → `tests/Feature/` mirroring the feature
- Unit tests → `tests/Unit/` mirroring the class
- Avoid generic `Helpers/` / `Utils/` dumps — use Action or Service
